Subject: [PATCH] wifi: realtek: resolve includes through Kbuild's source directory

The vendor drivers assume that $(src) is relative to the current working
directory. In a separate O= output tree it is relative to the kernel source,
so compilation fails on drv_types.h and nested PHYDM/HAL makefile includes.

Use kbuild-dir, which scripts/Makefile.build already resolves from srctree
and src before including each driver Makefile. This also handles absolute
source directories used by external modules. Keep all enabled vendor Wi-Fi
drivers and their existing feature configuration.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [compatibility with the pinned vendor kernel]

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/rtl8189es/Makefile b/drivers/net/wireless/rtl8189es/Makefile
index faa4c0c..cc5e2cf 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rtl8189es/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rtl8189es/Makefile
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ ifeq ($(GCC_VER_49),1)
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -Wno-date-time	# Fix compile error && warning on gcc 4.9 and later
 endif
 
-EXTRA_CFLAGS += -I$(src)/include
+EXTRA_CFLAGS += -I$(kbuild-dir)/include
 
 EXTRA_LDFLAGS += --strip-debug
 
@@ -249,10 +249,10 @@ _HAL_INTFS_FILES :=	hal/hal_intf.o \
 			hal/led/hal_$(HCI_NAME)_led.o
 
 
